                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "EDIT: PLEASE avoid this game at all costs. \n\nI've done some more \"research\" and there are a few more concerning things I've found. \n\n1. This game was released on Android in 2013.\n2. This game was released as a full complete game on Desura in early 2014. The price? $3.99.\n3. The last post on the Dev's website? Announcement of Greenlt status. Before that? 2013 was the last post.\n4. The dev's contact is a twitter account. The last activity on the twitter account? 2014.\n5. Zero contact, messaging, updates, responses to negative reviews/posts since the game released.\n\nEnd EDIT.\n\nUnfortunetly, this game is not very good.\n\nVery simplistic platforming. At about level 5 when you get to the end of the level nothing happens. But considering how fast you can get there (2-4 minutes) plus the fact that there are only 13 levels (Supposedly) mean this game is probably not more then 30 mins of gameplay. No difficulty levels or anything. So thats $10.00 for about 30 mins of gameplay or to put it another way it's about $20 an hour. Considering how many games I've bought for $50 and played for more than 50 hours ($1.00 an hour), I don't think it's a very good deal.\n\nBefore my next observation, I would like to preface it with the fact that, overall, I am a big fan of the early access system. Prison Architect, The Forest and Stranded Deep are a few examples.\n\nThat being said, this game appears to be abandoned. Released on May 25th and not a word or sign of the dev. In my opinion, especially at the $10.00 price tag, this is just a money grab. Dev, please prove me wrong.\n\nI ABSOLUTELY DO NOT recommend buying this game. At a quarter of the price it would still be overpriced.",
